# Moby occlusion census rows (tests/harness/check_moby_occlusion.sh).
# Rows: <name> | <level> | <freecam pose> | <checks>
# checks, space-separated:
#   max_ratio=R   the extended leg's sub-tick simple-kind triangles are at most
#                 R times the original leg's (the extended reveal admits no
#                 hidden record into the decode)
#   unchanged     the extended leg's sub-tick simple-kind triangles equal the
#                 reference leg's (OPENPETE_MOBY_SIMPLE_OCCL=0): the visible
#                 extension is kept
#   engage        the extended leg's occlusion cull culls at least one record
#                 of either kind
#   report        no count criterion; the census is printed
#   sector_visibility=MODE
#                 every leg runs with --sector-visibility MODE
# Every row also requires every screenshot of the extended leg to be
# byte-identical to the reference leg's.
#
# colossus_wall: the reported pose, staring at a wall. Before simple-kind
# records took the occlusion test the extended leg decoded 123 simple records,
# 4,106 vertices and 3,985 triangles per sub-tick present against 8 / 75 / 53
# at original LOD, with an identical image.
# colossus_open: the same position turned to open space, where the extension
# is visible (394 simple triangles extended against 243 original).
# idol_springs_terrain: looking down at terrain; 6-14 animated records hidden
# behind it are drawn at both LODs (canonical-queued records, which a headless
# run keeps on every present). Under filled (the Spyro 2 default) and game
# sector visibility the moby path feeds nothing at this pose, so no sub-tick
# replay runs; the row runs frustum, which admits the hidden records.
colossus_wall        | colossus     | pos=(47666, 60635, 12089) yaw=78 pitch=41     | max_ratio=2 engage
colossus_open        | colossus     | pos=(47666, 60635, 12089) yaw=2126 pitch=41   | unchanged
idol_springs_terrain | idol_springs | pos=(115428, 98127, 14292) yaw=-1135 pitch=900 | report sector_visibility=frustum
